    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the favorable matchup against Peter Lambert, who is allowing us to aggressively start **Dylan Beavers** (61.18) and **Taylor Ward** (54.23). **Dylan Beavers** stands out as our premier play due to a strong combination of order positioning and a favorable platoon advantage, while **Tyler Freeman** (65.30) earns a high mark despite a lower lineup slot; the combination of a significant park boost and the chance to exploit the 4.47 xERA of Brady Singer makes him a critical utility start. We are also leaning on **Masyn Winn** (64.01), whose score is buoyed by a substantial 19% SP skill advantage against Merrill Kelly, and **Lawrence Butler** (59.78), who leverages a massive 13% dynamic platoon boost to overcome a moderate park environment and mitigate the threat posed by Cade Cavalli.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luis Arraez** (45.51). While he remains a consistent contributor, the optimizer strictly prioritized our need for speed and power upside against the difficult 2.85 xERA profile of Bryce Miller. **Luis Arraez** was ultimately edged out by the higher efficiency scores of **Gavin Sheets** and **Tyler Freeman**, both of whom are projected to capitalize on weaker pitching environments. We must keep a close watch on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Geraldo Perdomo**; their efficiency scores are highly sensitive to their confirmed batting order positions. Should any of these players move down the order following the final lineup release, we risk seeing their efficiency ratings dip below the 40-point threshold, necessitating a quick pivot to preserve our remaining game caps.",
